# Cecil, Dark Knight: "Whenever Cecil deals damage, you lose that much life." Combat damage to two blockers is dealt
# at once (CR 510.2), so Cecil deals damage once, not twice: one trigger waits on the stack and Bot1 loses the total, 2
# (1 deathtouch damage to each of two Ornithopters, lethal to both), not two separate 1s. Bot1 stays at 18, above half
# of 20, so Cecil does not transform.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Cecil, Dark Knight
Swamp x5
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Plains x5
Plains x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Cecil, Dark Knight.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Cecil, Dark Knight)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Cecil, Dark Knight; Ornithopter > Cecil, Dark Knight)
Bot1.AssignDamage(Cecil, Dark Knight > Ornithopter#1: 1; Cecil, Dark Knight > Ornithopter#2: 1)
? Stack.Count = 1
? Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 2
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Life = 18

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Cecil, Dark Knight.Tapped = true
